378 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line chart comparing mean acceptability of ChatGPT functions between students and teachers on a one to five Likert scale. Students rate all functions higher, especially for brainstorming, outlining, and editing, than teachers, who rate drafting lowest. Error bars represent variability.) /K 420 0 R /P 54 0 R /Pg 11 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
379 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Horizontal bar chart comparing mean acceptability scores for various academic writing tasks between students and teachers. Brainstorming and outlining have the highest scores for both groups, while translation and drafting have the lowest. Green bars represent students and yellow bars represent teachers, with students consistently displaying higher acceptability scores, except for translation and drafting where both groups' scores are low. Key tasks listed are brainstorming, outlining, editing, summarizing, referencing, paraphrasing, translation, and drafting, with scores ranging from approximately 2.5 to 4.5.) /K 421 0 R /P 54 0 R /Pg 11 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
